{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundRunService.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:01.122597Z","id":"d6cba6c23f05fdbce358a213649d0f67196bebdddc989381f3e3cf494c7ca3d9","body":{"detail":"shortService needs no type permission but is cut at about 3 minutes from startForeground (Service.onTimeout, then an ANR mentioning FOREGROUND_SERVICE_TYPE_SHORT_SERVICE if not stopped), and can be extended only while the app is visible. One MessagesApiBackend attempt may take up to its 5-minute timeout (lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart:31), a make can be followed by a queued change, and both would be cut mid-run in the background. dataSync (FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC, a normal permission) allows 6 hours in 24 for apps targeting 35+, reset whenever the app comes to the foreground; onTimeout(int,int) stops the service if that is ever spent. Cost: a Play Console foreground-service-type declaration, and Android's guidance points dataSync users to user-initiated data transfer jobs.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":92},"end":{"line":106},"content_hash":"e125175dc61f9be9e1d11b4bca332738003edbb843ed09cafcb34d9388f65815"},"summary":"shortService instead of dataSync for the run service","tags":["revisit:Play review refuses the dataSync declaration, or Android restricts dataSync further (for example a lower daily limit)","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/MainActivity.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:01.122833Z","id":"241d5a60405532e121a442cadffa5ffd4bd83e542a795b92c17d79b78a1c4531","body":{"detail":"The Dart run lives in the activity's Flutter engine. Finishing the activity (back from the launcher) or removing the task (BackgroundRunService.onTaskRemoved) ends the engine, so the run stops and the service is stopped with it; a change is recovered by the feedback worker on the next start, but a new app's request is gone and no notice says so. The service keeps the process alive, not the engine.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":72},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"8bce7baf24ad3c4c40388650f474793b85b25fde3909c096977fc129ff495a20"},"suggested_fix":"Run the agent on a FlutterEngine owned by the service or the Application (a cached engine), or post a 'stopped' notice from onTaskRemoved when a make was running.","summary":"A make in flight is lost when the activity is finished or the task is swiped away","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundWorkChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:01.122903Z","id":"da2ee5a94fc6a9cc01e54c52146223de857bc863028e33226b470c57e6b47ed0","body":{"detail":"requestPermission asks at the first Make (lib/app.dart:477) and records asked_post_notifications in shared preferences, so a person who dismissed the dialog never sees the ready notices and is not told why. The foreground service still runs (its notification shows only in the task manager).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":90},"end":{"line":112},"content_hash":"c12b6a1d8ad8bd3a524949912c51e4f0acfaedb545dab65aadee3422c75c083a"},"suggested_fix":"Show a Settings row for notifications that opens the app's settings page (openAppSettings) when they are off.","summary":"POST_NOTIFICATIONS is asked for once per install; after a denial nothing in the app offers it again","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundRunService.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:01.123010Z","id":"5249ca0f6c622f571cc227c945b703a3324bc929f14436f6823e4f96c30bbefc","body":{"detail":"flutter build apk --debug compiles BackgroundRunService and BackgroundWorkChannel and the APK's manifest declares the dataSync service and its permissions; test/app_background_test.dart and test/platform/background_work_test.dart drive the Dart side against a fake BackgroundWork and a mocked channel. Not yet observed on a phone: that the service keeps the network up in the background (no blocked=APP_BACKGROUND in dumpsys netpolicy during a run), the permission dialog, the notification's look, and that tapping a ready notice opens that artifact (cold and warm).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":92},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"017b7990d75a36045d4a1f44899b8297de344f1390c2efc3ea541bac5514235d"},"summary":"The service and notices are checked only by the debug build compiling and by fake-channel tests, not on a device","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundWorkChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:27:37.268286Z","id":"d7022eb2e3ea61322c57218bd21d2e2dc72beda1081796f6fc50eba185d70bad","body":{"detail":"BackgroundRuns.begin and end (lib/platform/background_work.dart:206-241) send start and stop unawaited, back to back when a run ends at once (a Cancel or back press right after Make, a backend that throws before any network call, a scripted run). If the stop message is already on the main looper when start is handled, stopService runs before BackgroundRunService.onStartCommand. AOSP ActiveServices.bringDownServiceLocked (frameworks/base main, 'Bringing down service while still waiting for start foreground') then sends SERVICE_FOREGROUND_CRASH_MSG, which crashes the process with 'Context.startForegroundService() did not then call Service.startForeground()'. Separately, an exception from startForeground at BackgroundRunService.kt:102 (ForegroundServiceStartNotAllowedException, or a missing type permission) is uncaught in onStartCommand and also kills the process, taking the Dart run with it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":73},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"dd1d0a6f46f2156634ddb35fdcca587479720bfe30747d725a1c3922e755da89"},"suggested_fix":"Stop through the service: deliver stop as an intent action to onStartCommand (or set a companion stopRequested flag that onStartCommand checks right after startForeground), so startForeground always runs before stopSelf. Wrap startForeground in try/catch and stopSelf on failure.","summary":"stop can reach the service before its onStartCommand has called startForeground, which crashes the app","tags":["review","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/MainActivity.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:27:37.268498Z","id":"5f5de109dc2755908ebdddfdcaab4b4961ec8d4874817915f18130b9a92cb581","body":{"detail":"Flutter's PlatformPlugin.popSystemNavigator calls activity.finish() for an activity that is not an OnBackPressedDispatcherOwner (FlutterActivity is not), so a back press on the home screen while a change runs reaches onDestroy with isFinishing, stops the service and destroys the engine with the Dart run. Mitigations: override popSystemNavigator() in MainActivity to moveTaskToBack(true) and return true, which keeps the activity, engine and run alive on back. For a swiped-away make, persist the pending make's request when it begins and clear it when it ends; on the next launch offer to make it again. A change is already recovered from the change ledger and the stranded-thread recheck.","kind":"comment","references":"241d5a60405532e121a442cadffa5ffd4bd83e542a795b92c17d79b78a1c4531","span":{"start":{"line":72},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"8bce7baf24ad3c4c40388650f474793b85b25fde3909c096977fc129ff495a20"},"summary":"Back from the home screen also finishes the activity, so this loss is not only a swipe-away; both have cheap mitigations","tags":["review","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundRunService.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:27:37.268546Z","id":"8ce145a5e541bce93c8b629041f9d313e4fd44f0917ccc87d2542b4cbd94d71b","body":{"detail":"The service is started from the visible activity at Make and at a change's WorkerWorking, which the foreground-start rules allow. dataSync has no time limit on Android 14 and 6 h per 24 h on Android 15 and later; onTimeout(int, int) stops it, as the platform requires within seconds. shortService's 3-minute limit would cut long tool-loop runs. A foreground service lifts the APP_BACKGROUND block: NetworkPolicyManager.isProcStateAllowedNetworkWhileBackground (frameworks/base main, core/java/android/net/NetworkPolicyManager.java:855-861) allows procState < PROCESS_STATE_TOP_SLEEPING, and FOREGROUND_SERVICE is below it. Google Play requires a dataSync declaration and may retire the type in favour of user-initiated data transfer jobs; neither applies to a sideloaded build today.","kind":"comment","references":"d6cba6c23f05fdbce358a213649d0f67196bebdddc989381f3e3cf494c7ca3d9","span":{"start":{"line":92},"end":{"line":106},"content_hash":"e125175dc61f9be9e1d11b4bca332738003edbb843ed09cafcb34d9388f65815"},"summary":"dataSync holds up for Android 14 to 16 as used here","tags":["review","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundWorkChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:13:19.448730Z","id":"19c2d535623ea174769b0b63d7c88d8c5b5976c138daedcbef1aa0b8f841da8a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"stop is now an ACTION_STOP command delivered through startService (BackgroundWorkChannel.kt 'stop', MainActivity.onDestroy), so BackgroundRunService.onStartCommand handles it after any queued start's startForeground, and stops only via stopSelfResult(startId) so a newer queued start is kept; startForeground is wrapped in try/catch and a refusal stops the service and reports 'stopped'. Evidence: flutter build apk --debug exit 0, dex contains dev.empathic.clax.STOP_RUNS. Not yet exercised on a device (see 5249ca0f).","supersedes":"d7022eb2e3ea61322c57218bd21d2e2dc72beda1081796f6fc50eba185d70bad","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/MainActivity.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:13:19.450239Z","id":"937de3a0f3ca8b65d56c164bf33415cd7f77aceb6c04a76908f1c2e9a0c36687","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Back no longer finishes the activity: MainActivity.popSystemNavigator moves the task to the back and keeps the engine and its run (f1c07f346b12). A make cut off by a swipe-away or process death is offered again: AppRoot keeps its request in pending-make.json (lib/platform/pending_make.dart) until it ends, and at the next launch asks 'Make it again?' (f1c07f346b12). The run itself is still lost on swipe-away; it is not resumed. Evidence: flutter test test/app_background_test.dart -> +11 all passed, including 'a make the last run never finished is offered again at launch' and 'Not now forgets the lost make'; test/platform/pending_make_test.dart passed.","supersedes":"241d5a60405532e121a442cadffa5ffd4bd83e542a795b92c17d79b78a1c4531","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundRunService.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:06:58.413393Z","id":"547296821176ccafd0bdaad4d0ea64f29da7f5b507ce7bce9d89d405adacdb2a","body":{"detail":"When startForeground throws in onStartCommand (Android 15 dataSync time spent: ActiveServices.setServiceForegroundInnerLocked clears fgRequired and then throws ForegroundServiceStartNotAllowedException), stopOnItsOwn calls stopSelf(), which stops the service whatever start IDs are queued. If a second start from startForegroundService is already queued, its fgRequired is set again and the bring-down crashes the app ('did not then call Service.startForeground'). It needs that refusal plus a second run starting within the same moment, so it is rare.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":124},"content_hash":"0388ce42b0570e7dcdc42fcc7309f2f4e64feba609213be472630de227671943"},"suggested_fix":"In the onStartCommand failure path, stop with stopSelfResult(startId) so a newer queued start still runs; keep stopSelf() for onTimeout and onTaskRemoved.","summary":"A refused startForeground stops with stopSelf(), which also drops a start queued after it","tags":["review","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundRunService.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:08:10.991640Z","id":"089b1c012e45c512ae633f9f9787a191e99b1bfc79dcd0ef415f166787775791","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The refused-startForeground path in BackgroundRunService.onStartCommand now calls stopSelfResult(startId) and reports 'stopped' only when the service did stop, so a start queued after it gets its own startForeground. Evidence: flutter build apk --debug exit 0.","supersedes":"547296821176ccafd0bdaad4d0ea64f29da7f5b507ce7bce9d89d405adacdb2a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/CuesChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:08:55.223065Z","id":"0181ecc6f17c3609f541e6d74c692bf32288999394c4534758df2efa42551ac2","body":{"detail":"AOSP ToneGenerator.cpp defines TONE_PROP_BEEP as one 40 ms burst of 400+1200 Hz and TONE_PROP_ACK as 100 ms of 1200 Hz, 100 ms off, repeated once (two bursts, about 300 ms). play() calls startTone(tone, DURATION_MS) with DURATION_MS = 120, which stops ACK after its first burst: the start is a 40 ms blip and the stop a 100 ms blip in the same 1200 Hz band, not the double 'acknowledge' beep the stop was chosen for. The class comment's '120 ms tone' is also wrong for BEEP (40 ms). Keep the start short (it plays as the recognizer opens the microphone) and let the stop play whole: startTone(tone) without a duration (both tones are finite), or a duration of at least 300 ms for ACK, and release after the longest tone plus slack. TONE_PROP_BEEP2 (two 40 ms bursts 200 ms apart) is an alternative stop.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"e1f1cd456dcaceff7626e073ea558a30e8a6f66e8920ef04409e2cd5ee4001ee"},"suggested_fix":"Play ACK in full (startTone(tone) or a 320 ms duration), release after ~500 ms, and correct the class comment's durations.","summary":"The stop tone is cut to one burst, so start and stop tones differ little","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/CuesChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:10:59.968353Z","id":"bd1d867f277b68faf86c503a5f9e1113c577aae461fe6453f0f3eeb24c0c4ef6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"CuesChannel.kt plays TONE_PROP_ACK for 320 ms (both bursts) to stop and the single short TONE_PROP_BEEP (60 ms cap) to start, releases the generator after 500 ms, and its class comment states each tone. flutter build apk --debug: exit 0, CuesChannel.class rebuilt.","supersedes":"0181ecc6f17c3609f541e6d74c692bf32288999394c4534758df2efa42551ac2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/AppNoticeChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:04:23.183025Z","id":"56d5a66f4f167d9079c22db420da871b1e1ecdb4c2322b3464b6133fdedff09b","body":{"detail":"Unverified on a device: (1) the notification is silent with no heads-up on the IMPORTANCE_LOW \"open_app\" channel; (2) tapping Comment or Threads collapses the shade and reaches MainActivity.onNewIntent as single top, so test/app_test.dart's routing is what the phone does; (3) pulling the shade down reports AppLifecycleState.inactive, not paused, so apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart _tellVisible keeps the notice while the shade is open (it clears on hidden/paused); (4) on Android 14 and later an ongoing notification of an app without a foreground service can be swiped away, and the screen posts it again only when it next comes to the front; (5) AppNoticeChannel.allowed reads a channel the person turned off as not allowed, so the edge handle comes back.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":133},"end":{"line":156},"content_hash":"29a899e32459b06ef6588f594c941748eded3d109350f7b575eb6dd92ca96673"},"suggested_fix":"On the phone: open an app, pull the shade, tap Comment and Threads, swipe the notice away, turn the open_app channel off and on in system settings, and press Home; note each result here.","summary":"The open app's notice is checked only by the Kotlin compiling (gradlew :app:compileDebugKotlin) and by fake-channel Dart tests, not on a phone","tags":["device","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/AppNoticeChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:07:48.262539Z","id":"4475790744600b7abdf6bbaab63f1a8f8aab10fcfc9b953f247a2231b6447ca2","body":{"detail":"Since Android 14 an ongoing notification that is not a foreground service's is dismissible by the user. show() sets no delete intent, so Dart never learns of the dismissal: allowed() (line 108) still answers true, so apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart keeps the edge handle hidden (it shows only when _noticeAllowed == false), and _showNotice (app_screen.dart:315-331) reposts only on the next visibility change. The only way in left is the undiscoverable two-finger swipe. Unverified on a device (see 56d5a66f).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":133},"end":{"line":156},"content_hash":"29a899e32459b06ef6588f594c941748eded3d109350f7b575eb6dd92ca96673"},"suggested_fix":"Add setDeleteIntent (a broadcast or activity PendingIntent) that tells Dart the notice was dismissed; the screen then shows the edge handle, or reposts on the next resume.","summary":"On Android 14 and later the person can swipe the open app's notice away, and then nothing shows the way into comment mode until the app screen leaves and returns","tags":["review","u7","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/AppNoticeChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:07:48.262680Z","id":"69aef3bd39d29e4598e28c495b23c49e83dd92f546209bd1f8b15704266ea2ce","body":{"detail":"Both build Intent(context, MainActivity) with no action or data, so Intent.filterEquals tells them apart only by request code: 7410-7412 here, artifact.hashCode() in BackgroundRunService.kt:41-51. An artifact ID hashing to 7410-7412 would make FLAG_UPDATE_CURRENT rewrite one notification's extras with the other's. Unlikely, but a per-action Intent action (and the artifact as data) removes it and makes the codes unique per app too.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"24f242dd648b62841daf693c5891c7d4435085c51b625671d4e85b196f2d0a97"},"summary":"Give the notice's PendingIntents an action or data URI so they cannot collide with BackgroundRunService.open's","tags":["review","u7","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/AppNoticeChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:11:33.675678Z","id":"342442b6c29636db9519ce93e726b43686bedcbe82e0c3d56975afec852cf407","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: the notice's delete intent (immutable broadcast to this package, ACTION_DISMISSED) calls `dismissed` {artifact}; AppScreen then shows the edge handle until it next comes to the front, which posts the notice again. flutter test test/ui/app_screen_test.dart --plain-name 'a swiped-away notice' passes; gradlew :app:compileDebugKotlin BUILD SUCCESSFUL. Device behaviour stays under 56d5a66f.","supersedes":"4475790744600b7abdf6bbaab63f1a8f8aab10fcfc9b953f247a2231b6447ca2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/AppNoticeChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:11:33.676696Z","id":"2a35789e8d8924c4c8f96adcceaf60142d2bfb5a0a1ec26d5655bd778d80847f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: the body, Comment and Threads intents carry ACTION_OPEN, ACTION_COMMENT and ACTION_THREADS (dev.empathic.clax.notice.*), so Intent.filterEquals never matches Notices.open's action-less intent. gradlew :app:compileDebugKotlin BUILD SUCCESSFUL.","supersedes":"69aef3bd39d29e4598e28c495b23c49e83dd92f546209bd1f8b15704266ea2ce","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BundleIntake.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:50:09.005459Z","id":"f25e7a27bf85a56f380f3744d0f9136d3e98c1a7a36e8afc048ba155f1a044b2","body":{"detail":"BundleIntake.kt copies each opened file to <cache>/incoming/<random>.clax and hands the path to Dart; nothing deletes it after Dart reads it, so a run that opens many bundles keeps each copy (at most 32 MiB each) until the activity is next created or Android trims the cache. lib/platform/bundle_intake.dart's OpenedBundle.file says the reader may delete an Android copy once read; the consumer in lib/app.dart can do that.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":51},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"81863eaca44483886c7cab778e6903c5863df37ae1efce05aaee6a70ef878fe0"},"summary":"Copies under <cache>/incoming/ are removed only when the next MainActivity is created","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BundleIntake.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:50:09.005533Z","id":"7219cb2700d0beaf2ce6e0294223820a645e2722410d159a441f56c7b311e8a0","body":{"detail":"Checked only by a debug APK build: the merged manifest in build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-debug.apk (aapt2 dump xmltree) carries the VIEW and SEND filters with the three MIME types, and the Kotlin compiles. Cold start (initial answered after the launching copy ends), onNewIntent while running, the 32 MiB refusal and the recents redelivery guard are untested on a device.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":97},"end":{"line":130},"content_hash":"919dd20fde2cdb392e45f221da9af6b931d4b84f47533b681f5e0ddfd31ffdea"},"summary":"The Android intake (intent filters and BundleIntake.kt) has run on no device","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BundleIntake.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:54:19.800968Z","id":"4e66210595d8cd7ec2f15e69f6208cfbae617844aeda9da7ec1a888462048034","body":{"detail":"Failure: any app shares or opens a content: URI whose provider throws IllegalArgumentException, IllegalStateException, NullPointerException or UnsupportedOperationException from openFile (Parcel.readException rethrows these in Clax), or a URI ContentResolver.openInputStream rejects with IllegalArgumentException. copy() catches only IOException and SecurityException (lines 122-128), so the exception escapes on the executor thread started at line 66, the default uncaught handler kills the process, and the main.post that decrements `copying` never runs. Catch Exception (or RuntimeException too) in copy(), and keep the decrement and deliver in a finally-equivalent path.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":97},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"18749f1b784876a09501f849695ac7dc9ec445d05cf623f43e9e7391ee3433fc"},"summary":"An unchecked exception from the sender's content provider crashes Clax and leaves `initial` unanswered","tags":["review","bp","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BundleIntake.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:54:19.801107Z","id":"6393892d9799f2d81ecfd7752d07b3cccf79b7ccf82195317131fae275149e6a","body":{"detail":"uriOf accepts file: URIs and copy() opens them with Clax's own permissions, so any installed app can send VIEW file:///data/user/0/<package>/... or content://dev.empathic.clax.flutter.share_provider/... (Clax's non-exported providers, readable by Clax itself) and Clax copies that private file to <cache>/incoming/ and hands it to the reader. Nothing returns to the sender, so the impact is low (at worst a kept bundle from the lineage store opens the import sheet unbidden), but refusing a file: path whose canonical form lies under applicationInfo.dataDir, and content: URIs whose authority is one of Clax's own, closes the confused-deputy path. Since Android 7 other apps cannot hand out file: URIs without FileUriExposedException, so dropping file: from uriOf and the VIEW filter costs little.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":137},"end":{"line":137},"content_hash":"2b029391390e9eb46b4cc9d69cd9d81f0311f3d7e6b9867e3b8744a9c63ef6f2"},"summary":"A file: (or Clax's own content:) URI from any app makes Clax copy one of its own private files into the intake","tags":["review","bp","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BundleIntake.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:54:19.801140Z","id":"b5bad8016608611ad71b2493790eb767efac2db33dca53ac05c9928881684688","body":{"detail":"copy() reads with a blocking src.read on the single-thread executor (line 32). A content provider that keeps its pipe open without writing never returns, so every later intent's copy queues behind it and, at cold start, `copying` stays above zero and Dart's `initial` (line 47) never gets an answer for the life of the process. Separately, a second `initial` arriving while a copy runs (a Dart hot restart) overwrites initialResult and leaves the first call unanswered. A per-copy deadline (or a cached thread pool with the cap still applied) and answering any replaced initialResult would bound both.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":78},"content_hash":"5a31250419740da7c4cc6a0711e48052abca13ea71e7a0dfa972793b22cbbdc0"},"summary":"One IO thread with no read timeout: a provider that never finishes stalls every later file and the `initial` answer","tags":["review","bp","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BundleIntake.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:54:19.801169Z","id":"b1dae092a0311fd956489d9489411d2e9f349ab78972a2cefee9b2ed4b768148","body":{"detail":"The typed Intent.getParcelableExtra(name, Class) has a framework defect on API 33 that androidx.core.content.IntentCompat.getParcelableExtra works around by calling it only when SDK_INT >= 34 and using the deprecated form below that. Switching the check at line 157 to 34 (or calling IntentCompat) avoids it on Android 13 devices.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"cf8ae9f8758fe9a739199ee7e790680052bf5076af08180298d910b9ddc53313"},"summary":"Use the typed getParcelableExtra only from API 34, as androidx IntentCompat does","tags":["review","bp","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BundleIntake.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:57:23.189622Z","id":"756a0ddbfdbd95a18778206ae150e7e9398ee9255f6e551de47ce27c2f798384","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: onNewIntent's IO job catches Exception around copy(), and always posts finish(), which decrements copying and answers initial when it reaches 0. flutter build apk --debug: EXIT 0 (target/bp-apk-build2.log).","supersedes":"4e66210595d8cd7ec2f15e69f6208cfbae617844aeda9da7ec1a888462048034","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BundleIntake.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:57:23.190886Z","id":"6c443409c775547655c15fe4c84db6cb7be3c53fb887619c12e4c734531b1e36","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: BundleIntake.acceptable takes content: URIs only and refuses an authority whose provider resolves to Clax's package (or starts with it); both BundleReceiverActivity and MainActivity's intake check it. The manifest's VIEW filter lists only scheme content (aapt2 dump of app-debug.apk). flutter build apk --debug: EXIT 0 (target/bp-apk-build2.log).","supersedes":"6393892d9799f2d81ecfd7752d07b3cccf79b7ccf82195317131fae275149e6a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BundleIntake.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:57:23.192139Z","id":"7eec39c21732a723a9c621af2133bfae52e7f25023d608ec20d5807925b249ce","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: each copy runs on its own thread of a cached pool under a COPY_TIMEOUT_MS (120 s) watchdog that closes the stream and refuses the file, so a stalled provider blocks no later file; every pending initial call is answered (initialResults). flutter build apk --debug: EXIT 0 (target/bp-apk-build2.log).","supersedes":"b5bad8016608611ad71b2493790eb767efac2db33dca53ac05c9928881684688","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BundleIntake.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:57:23.193781Z","id":"9f836ad8ce43be00a493dc395ae181686e8590f0494f5bd226f41fcf33373b9b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: streamOf uses the typed getParcelableExtra only from SDK_INT >= 34. flutter build apk --debug: EXIT 0 (target/bp-apk-build2.log).","supersedes":"b1dae092a0311fd956489d9489411d2e9f349ab78972a2cefee9b2ed4b768148","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/MainActivity.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:45:28.697273Z","id":"44801f5ac02a2149491f92dfa8c0214dec6774e6fd14eaab4b7321590d015daf","body":{"detail":"It compiles (flutter build apk --debug), but no phone was attached. Under webview_flutter_android's texture-layer composition the WebView sits in a wrapper view; whether WebView.draw on a software Canvas paints its content (not black or blank) there is unchecked. Failure would show as a blank or black snapshot on the next cold start, covering the home screen until shown. Check: after a launch, open the app's cache home/home-snapshot.bin (its PNG follows the first line) or look at the cold start.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":38},"end":{"line":62},"content_hash":"7cbb0609926f26b155bd98c67af89b38c3a176847c142afc70ef80c635c718ed"},"summary":"Android's snapshotWebView (WebView.draw into a bitmap) is unverified on a device","tags":["android","unverified-on-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/MainActivity.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:00:02.013244Z","id":"fb161dba85b2e9b74d485e4f5c86a0adfdbd924992dd745a7ff884d84cbfa4fa","body":{"detail":"Theme.Clax.Starting (res/values/styles.xml) draws res/drawable/splash_mark.xml, the mark 132 dp wide on the 288 dp canvas, and installSplashScreen() hands over at Flutter's first frame to ClaxSplash (lib/ui/splash.dart), which draws the mark 132 wide at the window's centre. Only renders compare them: target/flutter-app/shots/splash-android-phone-{light,dark}.png (the drawable rasterised over clax_bg in a 412 x 915 dp window) against ClaxSplash's splash-phone-{light,dark}.png differ only in anti-aliased edges and the rig's status and gesture bars. Not checked: API 29-30 (core-splashscreen's compat view) and API 31+ (the system splash) on a phone, the window centre under the status and navigation bars on API 29-34 where the app is not edge to edge, and the splash's exit fade.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"421088e85bd578f2ca86be93de60955152cb1a2f58ce770d7a758bca997bb489"},"suggested_fix":"On a phone, light and dark, on API 30 and 31+: record the launch and confirm the mark keeps its place and size from the system splash to ClaxSplash.","summary":"The splash's mark size and the jump to ClaxSplash are unverified on a device","tags":["phase:8","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/AppNoticeChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:34:40.434155Z","id":"41014a0b4e6e580e477f41054eefdfdc7d465b8bfe4aa6428a2d61e328dfac00","body":{"detail":"bazelisk build //apps/clax_app:apk compiles it; apps/clax_app/test/ui/app_screen_test.dart drives FakeAppNotice.turnOnAnswer. Unchecked on Android 13+: a second ask after one refusal (shouldShowRequestPermissionRationale), the settings page opening (ACTION_APP_NOTIFICATION_SETTINGS) and the answer arriving through MainActivity.onRequestPermissionsResult while BackgroundWorkChannel shares the asked_post_notifications preference.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":146},"content_hash":"9d9236e554f886a74578b45376b85edd42afa375a6e9179a2eea5e51536ee287"},"summary":"The hint's Turn on (turnOn: the POST_NOTIFICATIONS request, else the app's notification settings) is checked only by the Kotlin compiling and fake-notice Dart tests, not on a device","tags":["device","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundWorkChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:44:15.821100Z","id":"0e1225b704a6b52821ae280c62f2520b9c64ba2310c6a116cfbb6ddf01538ef4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: Settings › Notifications shows whether notifications are on (read again on resume), Open settings (openAppSettings on dev.empathic.clax/native) and Show the Comment tab; with them off the app screen shows the Comment tab. settings_test 'off, it says so; Open settings opens the app’s system settings, and coming back checks again' and comment_tab_test pass (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_settings_test //apps/clax_app:ui_comment_tab_test //apps/clax_app:ui_app_screen_test)","supersedes":"da2ee5a94fc6a9cc01e54c52146223de857bc863028e33226b470c57e6b47ed0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/SchemeHost.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:39:08.877929Z","id":"69268521cf575fbd7df63956393d4a00165fbca1d126819a3ef6a8190f7ffaca","body":{"detail":"WebResourceResponse's constructor throws IllegalArgumentException for a status in 300-399, so SchemeHost.response maps it to 502 Bad Gateway. Spec section 4.2 step 1 forwards If-None-Match, and the core answers 304 to a match; whether the WebView ever sends a conditional header to shouldInterceptRequest is unverified.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":269},"end":{"line":276},"content_hash":"ae6bd61c0d60b6d487fba109674fd2a6e824b1213b64fe80c781f286b2fbb463"},"suggested_fix":"In the Dart answerer (lib/core/scheme.dart), drop If-None-Match on Android, or answer a 304 as a 200 with the body, and never answer a scheme request with a redirect.","summary":"WebResourceResponse takes no 3xx status: a 304 or a redirect from the core is answered 502 on Android","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/SchemeHost.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:39:08.877965Z","id":"e58744654cd3ea269e7a755a496d9d469367f74d4a7cf10b0c4cdd8c39905e5a","body":{"detail":"webview_flutter_android's setNavigationDelegate sets a new WebViewClient on the WebView. After attach that removes SchemeHost's Client, so requests to *.clax.invalid reach the network (and fail to resolve) and commits stop being reported. The same holds on Apple for the navigation delegate (macos/Runner/SchemeHost.swift attach): the policy and the navigation numbers stop, and every shell document answers 403.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":93},"end":{"line":100},"content_hash":"d98e7e3ce9646a5b00eb1fc9eefb81009bd886a8d61274605d457045ef7e1733"},"suggested_fix":"Attach after the controller's setNavigationDelegate and never call it again on an attached WebView; or route the plugin's setNavigationDelegate through a hook.","summary":"attach wraps the WebViewClient the WebView has at that moment; a later setNavigationDelegate from Dart replaces the wrapper and the app's hosts go unanswered","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/SchemeHost.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.370546Z","id":"2dac26a66f6234557b2d4d5758a152b069d25ffdf62725c744b9dff6b1f9f9ff","body":{"detail":"Conditional headers: the WebView's HTTP cache never stores an intercepted response, so it sends none of its own, but a page's fetch may set If-None-Match or If-Modified-Since (neither is a forbidden header name), and spec section 2.3's frame table (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md:313-314) forwards If-Modified-Since too, so dropping If-None-Match alone leaves a 304 path; drop both on Android. Redirects: the content routes answer 308 for /v/<n> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs:75), for .../index.html (content.rs:236) and for a draft token without its slash (crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs:414), so a page's <a href=\"index.html\"> answers 502 on Android. Apple does no better: a probe of WKWebView on macOS 26.6.2 handing a 308 with Location to WKURLSchemeTask.didReceive showed WebKit does not follow it and renders the 308's body at the old URL. Fix in the answerer (Task 15, lib/core/scheme.dart): follow a redirect whose target has the same base inside the core (index.html to ./) and answer the target; answer a document request for /v/<n> with a 200 text/html meta refresh to the Location; anything else 3xx becomes 404; and the native response() keeps its 502 only as a backstop.","kind":"comment","references":"69268521cf575fbd7df63956393d4a00165fbca1d126819a3ef6a8190f7ffaca","summary":"Confirmed and wider: drop If-None-Match and If-Modified-Since on Android, and never answer any scheme request with a 3xx on either platform","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/SchemeHost.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.370781Z","id":"c3754481917b78b355f535b065692d1b8ce0d68d727dc67a416091197fee40f7","body":{"detail":"Apple: configuration-hook.patch (bazel/flutter/plugin_overlays/webview_flutter_wkwebview/3/) can add a second static hook, navigationDelegateHook: ((WKWebView, WKNavigationDelegate?) -> WKNavigationDelegate?), called in WebViewProxyAPIDelegate's setNavigationDelegate, so SchemeHost composes NavigationProxy with whatever delegate is set, whenever (KVO on navigationDelegate is the unpatched fallback). Android: no setter hook exists, so attach (SchemeHost.kt:93-110) re-wraps when view.webViewClient !== state.client instead of returning early, and the Dart WebView surface calls attach after each setNavigationDelegate through one helper. Losing the wrap fails closed today (Apple: no permit, so every shell document 403; Android: the hosts reach the network and fail to resolve), but on Apple it also drops the policy's refusal of shell-host navigations in subframes (SchemeHost.swift:217-227), which spec section 4.2 relies on. Test: in scheme_spike.dart call controller.setNavigationDelegate a second time after attach, then require phase 2 and phase 3 to commit a numbered shell and the framed shell to be refused; it fails if the hook is undone. The same file's attach also adds the ClaxHost user script again on each attach after a detach (SchemeHost.swift:118-127).","kind":"comment","references":"e58744654cd3ea269e7a755a496d9d469367f74d4a7cf10b0c4cdd8c39905e5a","summary":"Make the wrap independent of order: a patch hook on the plugin's delegate setter on Apple, a re-wrapping attach on Android, and a spike step that sets the delegate again after attach","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/SchemeHost.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:42.316713Z","id":"df6355c64c33ba6c7cab2dd479011163ce011983ad94a68e30de3b9cac790100","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12 as the reply c3754481 proposes: navigation-delegate-hook.patch adds FWFWebViewFlutterWKWebViewExternalAPI.navigationDelegateHook, called by the plugin's setNavigationDelegate, which apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/SchemeHost.swift sets to keep its NavigationProxy in front of every delegate set later; SchemeHost.kt's attach wraps the client again when it is not the host's; the ClaxHost user script is added once per WKUserContentController. The spike (f1c07f346b12) sets the navigation delegate again after attach and attaches again: with the SchemeHost.swift before f1c07f346b12 it failed at 'first load' (the shell's request unnumbered and answered 403, no commit reported); with it, it passes with a numbered shell and a refused framed shell on the Mac (50 runs), the simulator and the Android emulator.","supersedes":"e58744654cd3ea269e7a755a496d9d469367f74d4a7cf10b0c4cdd8c39905e5a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/SchemeHost.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:43.430909Z","id":"9ce928229c8de4ea7e4f41652cb437c38343b46b179b9f4cc2327c6ea48d1c4e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12 as the reply 2dac26a6 proposes: SchemeHost.swift's respond and SchemeHost.kt's response() answer any 3xx (or a status outside 100..599) as a 502 text/plain body naming the status and that it was a redirect, and plan Task 15 has the answerer forward neither If-None-Match nor If-Modified-Since (on Android, and on Apple as well, since a 304 is a 3xx the native side now refuses), follow a same-base redirect inside the core, answer a document request for /v/<n> with a meta refresh, and answer any other 3xx 404. The spike's redirectRefused (a 308 from the table, fetched by the frame) was false before on the Mac (the frame read status 308, body 'moved') and holds after on the Mac (50 runs), the simulator and the Android emulator.","supersedes":"69268521cf575fbd7df63956393d4a00165fbca1d126819a3ef6a8190f7ffaca","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/MainActivity.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T23:06:43.831962Z","id":"85bb6161e58cd8dc549a9f05eb5c70068d71051f1d8f4580f0787c56c977bd62","body":{"detail":"On the Android emulator (//apps/clax_app:apk at f1c07f346b12, Settings › Developer › Don't keep activities on), relaunching Clax after its MainActivity was destroyed attached the new activity to the cached engine (the same PID, Dart's main not run again), and the status bar's clock and icons were drawn white on the light background (target/flutter-app/shots/keep-alive-relaunch.png). drawEdgeToEdge (apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart:69) runs once per Dart main, and each activity gets a PlatformPlugin of its own. Re-applying it when an activity attaches (AppLifecycleState.resumed after detached on Android, or WindowCompat in MainActivity.onCreate) would cover it; the first launch was not compared, since the core did not open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"33d3f70c66939e56c1c59652ce8a85e80a691f1b50b2579cfa8e8153365f5700"},"summary":"A second activity on the kept engine draws the status bar's icons light on the light screen: the edge-to-edge mode and bar styles main.dart's drawEdgeToEdge set apply to the first activity only","tags":["android","ui","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundWorkChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T23:06:43.832005Z","id":"7e1e240b39107b871482b4ebfbb9d3f32caf79bc1f75ad89182891a39b79ed5a","body":{"detail":"ClaxApplication keeps the engine after MainActivity finishes; the channel handlers MainActivity.configureFlutterEngine installed stay on its messenger until the next activity installs its own. start, update, stop, ready and failed go through the application context, but requestPermission calls activity.requestPermissions on the finished activity, whose answer never comes (permissionResult waits), and 'dev.empathic.clax/native' starts activities from it. QueueKeepAlive asks requestPermission at each KeepAlive(true), so a job started while no activity is attached can leave the request hanging until the next one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":123},"content_hash":"940ac640523634aaecebfade6fa020572b3ada4e0c703047f4d8a27bd145d80c"},"summary":"While no activity is attached to the kept engine, requestPermission (and MainActivity's native channel) still run on the activity that was destroyed","tags":["android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/ClaxApplication.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T23:06:43.832038Z","id":"635d6867ac31de9707bcce0a0d2a89fa63fb18cc305ff62064b2d3b39bc97e14","body":{"detail":"The emulator check of spec §7.6 could not start a make: the embedded core does not open on Android (the core.lock blocker on crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs). What was seen on the emulator (//apps/clax_app:apk at f1c07f346b12): with Don't keep activities on, MainActivity was destroyed (wm_on_destroy_called) and the next launch attached to the same engine in the same process (PID 5265, one Dart main). The macOS run of integration_test/kill_resume_test.dart covers the resume itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":45},"content_hash":"fc8615bf89298adb9322d57b5b2986a2ab351450fe6170cc63d49e8d53d23f69"},"summary":"Back out of a running make, the progress notification staying and the make landing, and a make resuming after `am kill`, are unverified on Android","tags":["android","verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/ClaxApplication.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T23:58:20.724442Z","id":"56ef97c20ec4a45827087af67c8ccae14232ff145edaeb5a10a4fd43c594fff2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"635d6867ac31de9707bcce0a0d2a89fa63fb18cc305ff62064b2d3b39bc97e14","summary":"The core.lock blocker this check was stopped by is fixed in 0a8d4312d97d (flock through nix); the emulator run of Back during a make and resume after am kill is still to be made. A make there needs an API key: CLAX_SCRIPTED_TURNS (apps/clax_app/lib/queue/scripted_turns.dart) is read from Platform.environment, which an app started by the Android launcher or am start does not receive.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundWorkChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:46:16.740624Z","id":"f2b5d970e582b1f941ee50f13139ed7814c4fda68d3bc947ee33c6d1cbd8bfc2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7e1e240b39107b871482b4ebfbb9d3f32caf79bc1f75ad89182891a39b79ed5a","summary":"Addressed in f1c07f346b12, not yet run on a device: the channels are made once per engine (EngineChannels.kt, through ClaxApplication.channels) and MainActivity only attaches and detaches. requestPermission now asks through the activity on screen and answers whether notifications may be posted, without asking, when none is; a request whose activity is destroyed is answered at detach with areNotificationsEnabled(). dev.empathic.clax/native starts its activities from the application context with FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK, so it needs no activity. Checked by //apps/clax_app:apk_test building the APK (the runner's Kotlin compiles); the repository has no Kotlin unit test setup (no android/app/src/test), see the concern on EngineChannels.kt. Left for the owner to close after a device run.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BundleIntake.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:46:16.740907Z","id":"adbe1dd09eccea1199558ebc682f98923cd25357e69c73f7cb4dc85d8e0a4254","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f25e7a27bf85a56f380f3744d0f9136d3e98c1a7a36e8afc048ba155f1a044b2","summary":"Since f1c07f346b12 BundleIntake is made once per engine (EngineChannels.kt), so <cache>/incoming/ is cleaned when the process's first activity makes the engine's channels, not at each MainActivity; copies from the running process stay until the next process start.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/EngineChannels.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:46:16.741485Z","id":"02ed8f546fa1050996f7c527fe8f71f0b405b822eabda8be773873a0fc158c48","body":{"detail":"There is no Kotlin unit test setup (android/app/src has main, debug and profile, no test; BUILD.bazel builds no android_local_test), so nothing exercises: a WebView's requests still answered after MainActivity is recreated (EngineChannels keeps one SchemeHost for the engine), a notice tap that launches a second activity reaching Dart as 'opened' (BackgroundWorkChannel.attach), a bundle intent on a later activity (BundleIntake.attach), requestPermission with no activity on screen, and http://app.clax.invalid answered 403 (SchemeHost.kt:152). Verified only by the APK building.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":38},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"73882d630c9ed962f69d0aa2950fbcbd9c2ba56f549ec2cf28f688039feb4d79"},"suggested_fix":"On the emulator: open an app, rotate or resize past configChanges (or 'adb shell am kill' the activity with the engine kept), and check the page still loads; tap a ready notice with the app in the background; and load http://app.clax.invalid/ in a page. Or add a Robolectric android_local_test for EngineChannels and SchemeHost.intercept.","summary":"The per-engine channels and SchemeHost's 403 for non-https app hosts are checked only by the Kotlin compiling in //apps/clax_app:apk_test, not by a test or on a device","tags":["android","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/MainActivity.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T19:26:54.790989Z","id":"674e87c66767d68fe8950f01ef2a577749deb7164b444906cb4b3a572d1a2935","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Obsolete: f1c07f346b12 removes snapshotWebView from the native channel (apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/EngineChannels.kt) with the home screen's launch snapshot; nothing draws a WebView into a bitmap any more. git grep -n snapshotWebView -- apps/clax_app finds nothing.","supersedes":"44801f5ac02a2149491f92dfa8c0214dec6774e6fd14eaab4b7321590d015daf","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/AppNoticeChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T20:52:05.836053Z","id":"e17e635df906ca0306e3d960350aeae7effb3735360b35d91bd791d76ff3cfd9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Obsolete: f1c07f346b12 removes the first-run hint and with it AppNoticeChannel's turnOn (the POST_NOTIFICATIONS request and the notification-settings fallback), so no Turn on is left to check on a device. bazelisk test via `just test-affected f1c07f346b12` at f1c07f346b12: 136 tests pass, among them //apps/clax_app:ui_app_screen_test, //apps/clax_app:app_test, //apps/clax_app:ui_settings_test, //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_app_shots_test, //apps/clax_app:dart_analyze and //apps/clax_app:apk_test; `git grep -n -e first-run-hint -e firstRunHint -e turnOn -- apps/clax_app/lib apps/clax_app/android ':!*.qual'` finds nothing (exit 1).","supersedes":"41014a0b4e6e580e477f41054eefdfdc7d465b8bfe4aa6428a2d61e328dfac00","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/ShellCache.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:53:57.725298Z","id":"f33adf1e5fa11f555fc89a0f91762cc4c31ab7d0f008ac6366721b2e43e25640","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the core's headers for these files cannot be reproduced natively at build time without drift. The ETag is clax_http::http_cache::etag_of, a hash of Rust's std DefaultHasher (crates/clax-http/src/http_cache.rs:21-25), and Cache-Control is IMMUTABLE or REVALIDATE by the core's cfg!(debug_assertions) (crates/clax-server/src/shell/mod.rs static_file), so a bundled copy would still need its headers registered from the core's answers at run time; keeping the core's answers (ShellCache) gives the same bytes and headers by construction with no build change. Cost: the first launch after an install or an update that changes the shell's hashes has the core answer each file once (in the scheme worker, not on the UI isolate). Measured on macOS (integration_test/load_timing_test.dart): 21 of an app open's 28 requests answered natively, p50 0.03 ms each against 1.5 ms through the worker.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"9d8183134fdc23e35a08a2a69c2afb70a357ba08e485a8fd07244c6e38bed9b1"},"summary":"Bundle web/dist's shell files (_clax/shell/**, _clax/transport.js) in the APK and the Apple app bundles and answer them natively from the first launch, instead of keeping the core's own answers once it has given them","tags":["revisit:a device measurement shows the first launch's shell load (time to the home app's first ready) matters","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/SchemeHost.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:53:57.725385Z","id":"b41352ac6496f4853a2322cac56bb60a96c894e75ca5eacec7af00422d9d0375","body":{"detail":"Unverified at run time: shouldInterceptRequest queueing on the WebView IO thread and answering a parked next from there (MethodChannel.Result.success off the task queue's thread), the work channel on messenger.makeBackgroundTaskQueue(), eval posting to the main thread, the IO-thread numbering of main-frame requests under the state's lock (intercept), and ShellCache (ShellCache.kt) keeping, serving and persisting the core's immutable answers. The same paths on macOS pass integration_test/scheme_spike_test.dart and integration_test/load_timing_test.dart (native answers equal to the core's: _sameAsCore). The UI frame rate on a phone while an app or the home screen loads is unmeasured.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":172},"end":{"line":215},"content_hash":"e09fdb591372f0726535af52e3565b6c5a0a18b2216256434a2b59010a63a527"},"suggested_fix":"Run just app-integration --android (android_scheme_spike_test) on an emulator, and the launch measure (scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --android) on a device before and after this change.","summary":"The Android scheme host's pull model and native shell cache are compiled (bazelisk build //apps/clax_app:apk) but never run: no JVM test and no emulator or device run has exercised them","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BundleIntake.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:20:46.728140Z","id":"7d1a30a803e55ee8eabdb2d60464758a32f7489846494416a29132bcd180be21","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7219cb2700d0beaf2ce6e0294223820a645e2722410d159a441f56c7b311e8a0","summary":"Since db78d1efd/13d4c5f3f the intake also forwards links (BundleReceiverActivity → OPEN_LINK → {url}); that path has also run on no device or emulator. apk_test checks only that the filters (clax scheme; https clax.dev /a/.*/get with autoVerify) and flutter_deeplinking_enabled=false are in the APK's manifest. An emulator check: adb shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d 'clax:get?url=…'.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/EngineChannels.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:16:04.114893Z","id":"1043a064f6957b35b20f4ff920f9c8c399100e530965d23e403d658c27de6c8a","body":{"detail":"openAuth builds the Custom Tabs intent by hand (ACTION_VIEW with the android.support.customtabs.extra.SESSION extra set to a null binder), which is the protocol CustomTabsIntent.Builder writes without a session, to avoid a new Maven dependency in the Gradle and Bazel builds. It has opened no tab on a device: the Kotlin is checked only by compiling //apps/clax_app:apk.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":98},"end":{"line":111},"content_hash":"2bc2d983320ada42204eb7f113f41dc83a3a2bb9539a69201a8c15436515c166"},"summary":"androidx.browser's CustomTabsIntent for the sign-in page","tags":["area:remote","revisit:the sign-in tab needs a toolbar colour, a warm-up or a session callback","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/MainActivity.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:30:58.016994Z","id":"951ba0a8302a60fcdd011a81ca4c43097d7e0dac8fefc03a1da240526671c78a","body":{"detail":"Theme.Clax.Starting (res/values/styles.xml) draws res/drawable/splash_mark.xml, the mark 132 dp wide on the 288 dp canvas, and installSplashScreen() hands over at Flutter's first frame to ClaxSplash (lib/ui/splash.dart), which draws the mark 132 wide at the window's centre. Only renders compare them: target/flutter-app/shots/splash-android-phone-{light,dark}.png (the drawable rasterised over clax_bg in a 412 x 915 dp window) against ClaxSplash's splash-phone-{light,dark}.png differ only in anti-aliased edges and the rig's status and gesture bars. Not checked: API 29-30 (core-splashscreen's compat view) and API 31+ (the system splash) on a phone, the window centre under the status and navigation bars on API 29-34 where the app is not edge to edge, and the splash's exit fade.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":22},"content_hash":"421088e85bd578f2ca86be93de60955152cb1a2f58ce770d7a758bca997bb489"},"suggested_fix":"On a phone, light and dark, on API 30 and 31+: record the launch and confirm the mark keeps its place and size from the system splash to ClaxSplash.","summary":"The splash's mark size and the jump to ClaxSplash are unverified on a device","supersedes":"fb161dba85b2e9b74d485e4f5c86a0adfdbd924992dd745a7ff884d84cbfa4fa","tags":["phase:8","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/MainActivity.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:30:58.104103Z","id":"2e564d5712eeb9cdbe719c3f164383085544490c434cca125d0d7a939e0fdd78","body":{"detail":"On the Android emulator (//apps/clax_app:apk at f1c07f346b12, Settings › Developer › Don't keep activities on), relaunching Clax after its MainActivity was destroyed attached the new activity to the cached engine (the same PID, Dart's main not run again), and the status bar's clock and icons were drawn white on the light background (target/flutter-app/shots/keep-alive-relaunch.png). drawEdgeToEdge (apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart:69) runs once per Dart main, and each activity gets a PlatformPlugin of its own. Re-applying it when an activity attaches (AppLifecycleState.resumed after detached on Android, or WindowCompat in MainActivity.onCreate) would cover it; the first launch was not compared, since the core did not open.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"33d3f70c66939e56c1c59652ce8a85e80a691f1b50b2579cfa8e8153365f5700"},"summary":"A second activity on the kept engine draws the status bar's icons light on the light screen: the edge-to-edge mode and bar styles main.dart's drawEdgeToEdge set apply to the first activity only","supersedes":"85bb6161e58cd8dc549a9f05eb5c70068d71051f1d8f4580f0787c56c977bd62","tags":["android","ui","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/SchemeHost.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:30:58.199883Z","id":"813c9ae371faaca0da06f3c01e9153595ea2c3589bbfb486ef9fd8b025f5aacd","body":{"detail":"Unverified at run time: shouldInterceptRequest queueing on the WebView IO thread and answering a parked next from there (MethodChannel.Result.success off the task queue's thread), the work channel on messenger.makeBackgroundTaskQueue(), eval posting to the main thread, the IO-thread numbering of main-frame requests under the state's lock (intercept), and ShellCache (ShellCache.kt) keeping, serving and persisting the core's immutable answers. The same paths on macOS pass integration_test/scheme_spike_test.dart and integration_test/load_timing_test.dart (native answers equal to the core's: _sameAsCore). The UI frame rate on a phone while an app or the home screen loads is unmeasured.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":171},"end":{"line":214},"content_hash":"e09fdb591372f0726535af52e3565b6c5a0a18b2216256434a2b59010a63a527"},"suggested_fix":"Run just app-integration --android (android_scheme_spike_test) on an emulator, and the launch measure (scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --android) on a device before and after this change.","summary":"The Android scheme host's pull model and native shell cache are compiled (bazelisk build //apps/clax_app:apk) but never run: no JVM test and no emulator or device run has exercised them","supersedes":"b41352ac6496f4853a2322cac56bb60a96c894e75ca5eacec7af00422d9d0375","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/AppNoticeChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:41.380171Z","id":"f75f72e14e62c4123aa3f7bde7fb64e574b28a1e5f68a8487f4b38744b0fb8b2","body":{"detail":"Unverified on a device: (1) the notification is silent with no heads-up on the IMPORTANCE_LOW \"open_app\" channel; (2) tapping Comment or Threads collapses the shade and reaches MainActivity.onNewIntent as single top, so test/app_test.dart's routing is what the phone does; (3) pulling the shade down reports AppLifecycleState.inactive, not paused, so apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart _tellVisible keeps the notice while the shade is open (it clears on hidden/paused); (4) on Android 14 and later an ongoing notification of an app without a foreground service can be swiped away, and the screen posts it again only when it next comes to the front; (5) AppNoticeChannel.allowed reads a channel the person turned off as not allowed, so the edge handle comes back.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":181},"end":{"line":205},"content_hash":"19281eade39fc3ae5afa4fd561dfc4392408e49cd34fcfef3f7b8372d7c7bc4d"},"suggested_fix":"On the phone: open an app, pull the shade, tap Comment and Threads, swipe the notice away, turn the open_app channel off and on in system settings, and press Home; note each result here.","summary":"The open app's notice is checked only by the Kotlin compiling (gradlew :app:compileDebugKotlin) and by fake-channel Dart tests, not on a phone","supersedes":"56d5a66f4f167d9079c22db420da871b1e1ecdb4c2322b3464b6133fdedff09b","tags":["device","unverified","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundRunService.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:41.484680Z","id":"5e3df79b1c1cf54badc192cb03740e8eced585af70494472cd2fe263aed7e050","body":{"detail":"flutter build apk --debug compiles BackgroundRunService and BackgroundWorkChannel and the APK's manifest declares the dataSync service and its permissions; test/app_background_test.dart and test/platform/background_work_test.dart drive the Dart side against a fake BackgroundWork and a mocked channel. Not yet observed on a phone: that the service keeps the network up in the background (no blocked=APP_BACKGROUND in dumpsys netpolicy during a run), the permission dialog, the notification's look, and that tapping a ready notice opens that artifact (cold and warm).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"b98e8913868d0aea13847d5cdb9efc34dd05402996281c91d1bd006566c205bf"},"summary":"The service and notices are checked only by the debug build compiling and by fake-channel tests, not on a device","supersedes":"5249ca0f6c622f571cc227c945b703a3324bc929f14436f6823e4f96c30bbefc","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundRunService.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:41.587408Z","id":"222a373582ff671ecbd3431ffc9461760c74fddb91694fec9243790e9703f888","body":{"detail":"shortService needs no type permission but is cut at about 3 minutes from startForeground (Service.onTimeout, then an ANR mentioning FOREGROUND_SERVICE_TYPE_SHORT_SERVICE if not stopped), and can be extended only while the app is visible. One MessagesApiBackend attempt may take up to its 5-minute timeout (lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart:31), a make can be followed by a queued change, and both would be cut mid-run in the background. dataSync (FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC, a normal permission) allows 6 hours in 24 for apps targeting 35+, reset whenever the app comes to the foreground; onTimeout(int,int) stops the service if that is ever spent. Cost: a Play Console foreground-service-type declaration, and Android's guidance points dataSync users to user-initiated data transfer jobs.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"4b835f5b7cd349ba31c3e3dd730d628834977753e345c73817d0e26608bcd772"},"summary":"shortService instead of dataSync for the run service","supersedes":"d6cba6c23f05fdbce358a213649d0f67196bebdddc989381f3e3cf494c7ca3d9","tags":["revisit:Play review refuses the dataSync declaration, or Android restricts dataSync further (for example a lower daily limit)","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundWorkChannel.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:41.691642Z","id":"42956813fb354943b139534cffbd4c130e57a78acd0a78991c86d29003df03a3","body":{"detail":"ClaxApplication keeps the engine after MainActivity finishes; the channel handlers MainActivity.configureFlutterEngine installed stay on its messenger until the next activity installs its own. start, update, stop, ready and failed go through the application context, but requestPermission calls activity.requestPermissions on the finished activity, whose answer never comes (permissionResult waits), and 'dev.empathic.clax/native' starts activities from it. QueueKeepAlive asks requestPermission at each KeepAlive(true), so a job started while no activity is attached can leave the request hanging until the next one.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":124},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"7933229146a2ddc3761214b42b8037c96938efe52577c3ec4d70029bf6c3e96f"},"summary":"While no activity is attached to the kept engine, requestPermission (and MainActivity's native channel) still run on the activity that was destroyed","supersedes":"7e1e240b39107b871482b4ebfbb9d3f32caf79bc1f75ad89182891a39b79ed5a","tags":["android","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/ClaxApplication.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:41.793940Z","id":"2b746e26789d6c3ebf5cacaa5cb98ccde3a260d1a745d8abe354e0c1bf1e3fc4","body":{"detail":"The emulator check of spec §7.6 could not start a make: the embedded core does not open on Android (the core.lock blocker on crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs). What was seen on the emulator (//apps/clax_app:apk at f1c07f346b12): with Don't keep activities on, MainActivity was destroyed (wm_on_destroy_called) and the next launch attached to the same engine in the same process (PID 5265, one Dart main). The macOS run of integration_test/kill_resume_test.dart covers the resume itself.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"b3ef5fcd7b8911c9eef8820241d0eb2f62c9d9b346c2b593bff57e406d96c028"},"summary":"Back out of a running make, the progress notification staying and the make landing, and a make resuming after `am kill`, are unverified on Android","supersedes":"635d6867ac31de9707bcce0a0d2a89fa63fb18cc305ff62064b2d3b39bc97e14","tags":["android","verification","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/EngineChannels.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:41.899369Z","id":"00028ff2dd0c860b78ff68e683e41a523f59f86ce4ac4e6cf266d0802167b7bd","body":{"detail":"There is no Kotlin unit test setup (android/app/src has main, debug and profile, no test; BUILD.bazel builds no android_local_test), so nothing exercises: a WebView's requests still answered after MainActivity is recreated (EngineChannels keeps one SchemeHost for the engine), a notice tap that launches a second activity reaching Dart as 'opened' (BackgroundWorkChannel.attach), a bundle intent on a later activity (BundleIntake.attach), requestPermission with no activity on screen, and http://app.clax.invalid answered 403 (SchemeHost.kt:152). Verified only by the APK building.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":37},"end":{"line":146},"content_hash":"8d283f98fdef9fdda6492c48e3d8ea116955c071a704d814d8da6179769b3be8"},"suggested_fix":"On the emulator: open an app, rotate or resize past configChanges (or 'adb shell am kill' the activity with the engine kept), and check the page still loads; tap a ready notice with the app in the background; and load http://app.clax.invalid/ in a page. Or add a Robolectric android_local_test for EngineChannels and SchemeHost.intercept.","summary":"The per-engine channels and SchemeHost's 403 for non-https app hosts are checked only by the Kotlin compiling in //apps/clax_app:apk_test, not by a test or on a device","supersedes":"02ed8f546fa1050996f7c527fe8f71f0b405b822eabda8be773873a0fc158c48","tags":["android","unverified","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BackgroundRunService.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:36:01.641961Z","id":"0524a6477c578787c7dd0cf5098637abc5a2a2d9b5531c13dbcea62073bf6c52","body":{"detail":"The service is started from the visible activity at Make and at a change's WorkerWorking, which the foreground-start rules allow. dataSync has no time limit on Android 14 and 6 h per 24 h on Android 15 and later; onTimeout(int, int) stops it, as the platform requires within seconds. shortService's 3-minute limit would cut long tool-loop runs. A foreground service lifts the APP_BACKGROUND block: NetworkPolicyManager.isProcStateAllowedNetworkWhileBackground (frameworks/base main, core/java/android/net/NetworkPolicyManager.java:855-861) allows procState < PROCESS_STATE_TOP_SLEEPING, and FOREGROUND_SERVICE is below it. Google Play requires a dataSync declaration and may retire the type in favour of user-initiated data transfer jobs; neither applies to a sideloaded build today.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"comment","references":"222a373582ff671ecbd3431ffc9461760c74fddb91694fec9243790e9703f888","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"4b835f5b7cd349ba31c3e3dd730d628834977753e345c73817d0e26608bcd772"},"summary":"dataSync holds up for Android 14 to 16 as used here","supersedes":"8ce145a5e541bce93c8b629041f9d313e4fd44f0917ccc87d2542b4cbd94d71b","tags":["review","android","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/BundleIntake.kt","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:39:12.268019Z","id":"be07999da44a58be4802777ecda063aa0ba6f5b21a1dc6186a92bf11666430f7","body":{"detail":"Checked only by a debug APK build: the merged manifest in build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-debug.apk (aapt2 dump xmltree) carries the VIEW and SEND filters with the three MIME types, and the Kotlin compiles. Cold start (initial answered after the launching copy ends), onNewIntent while running, the 32 MiB refusal and the recents redelivery guard are untested on a device.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":220},"end":{"line":237},"content_hash":"7ead876dcb5dc1406978057ffd209660ef328ef058b6c3e7650639a53418c0f2"},"summary":"The Android intake (intent filters and BundleIntake.kt) has run on no device","supersedes":"7219cb2700d0beaf2ce6e0294223820a645e2722410d159a441f56c7b311e8a0","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
